{
  "_comment": [
    "OPTIONAL — token-based Serro MCP wiring for CI or fully headless runs.",
    "",
    "The recommended path needs no file at all: register Serro once as a",
    "user-scoped server and let the Claude Code runtime own OAuth refresh:",
    "  claude mcp add --transport http --scope user serro https://mcp.serro.ai/mcp",
    "  claude mcp login serro",
    "",
    "Use this file only when that is not possible (CI, containers, no browser).",
    "To activate it:",
    "  1. cp .archon/mcp/serro.json.example .archon/mcp/serro.json",
    "  2. put SERRO_MCP_TOKEN=<token> in ~/.archon/.env  (NOT your repo .env —",
    "     Archon strips repo .env keys at boot so app secrets stay out of runs)",
    "  3. add  mcp: .archon/mcp/serro.json  to the workflow's serro-context node",
    "",
    "Archon expands $SERRO_MCP_TOKEN from its own process env. If the variable",
    "is undefined it warns and sends an empty bearer, which fails as a 401 —",
    "the context guard turns that into a clear run failure rather than a",
    "context-free answer."
  ],
  "serro": {
    "type": "http",
    "url": "https://mcp.serro.ai/mcp",
    "headers": {
      "Authorization": "Bearer $SERRO_MCP_TOKEN"
    }
  }
}
